  "reason": "1) Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_028: image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) yielding ~20.8% accuracy. This establishes a baseline but tells us nothing about whether the RNA modality contributes any signal. 2) Question: config_009 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, resnet50, weighted) directly tests whether adding an RNA representation (scGPT) to the same image backbone (ResNet50) and same profile setting improves over the image-only baseline. It isolates the multimodal contribution while holding image encoder and profile setting constant. 3) Why best: With only one data point, the highest-uncertainty decision is whether RNA adds value at all. scGPT is a learned biological representation giving RNA its best chance to contribute; weighted fusion is the simplest combination strategy, so a positive result is informative and a negative result is strong. This single experiment tells us whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal exploration or refocus on image-only improvements (encoder choice, multiprofile aggregation)."
}

